╭─ Issue description ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Issue Title: [Bug]: ToolResponse corrupts padded base64 chunks when merging streaming DataBlocks                                                │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ Description:                                                                                                                                    │
│ ### Prerequisites                                                                                                                               │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ -  I have searched the existing (https://github.com/agentscope-ai/agentscope/issues) and                                                        │
│ (https://github.com/agentscope-ai/agentscope/discussions), and this is not a duplicate.                                                         │
│ -  This is a bug, not a usage question. (For questions, please use                                                                              │
│ [Discussions](https://github.com/agentscope-ai/agentscope/discussions/new?category=general) instead.)                                           │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ ### Background / Description                                                                                                                    │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ `ToolResponse.append_chunk` corrupts streaming binary outputs when merging multiple `DataBlock` chunks with the same block id.                  │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ Currently, when both blocks use `Base64Source`, AgentScope merges them by directly concatenating the base64 strings. This works only when the   │
│ strings happen to have no padding. When each streamed chunk is independently base64-encoded and contains padding, the final merged payload      │
│ becomes invalid or decodes to incomplete bytes.                                                                                                 │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ Expected behavior: when both chunks contain valid base64 data, AgentScope should decode each chunk, concatenate the bytes, and re-encode the    │
│ merged bytes as one valid base64 string.                                                                                                        │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ I searched existing issues/discussions and did not find a duplicate report for this `ToolResponse` / `DataBlock` / base64 chunk merging issue.  │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ ### Error Messages                                                                                                                              │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ ```shell                                                                                                                                        │
│ The merged base64 string becomes:                                                                                                               │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ aGVsbG8=d29ybGQ=                                                                                                                                │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ Decoding this value recovers only the first padded segment:                                                                                     │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ b'hello'                                                                                                                                        │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ Expected decoded bytes:                                                                                                                         │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ b'helloworld'                                                                                                                                   │
│ ```                                                                                                                                             │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ ### Steps to Reproduce                                                                                                                          │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ 1. Run the following code:                                                                                                                      │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ ```python                                                                                                                                       │
│ import base64                                                                                                                                   │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ from agentscope.message import Base64Source, DataBlock                                                                                          │
│ from agentscope.tool import ToolChunk, ToolResponse                                                                                             │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ response = ToolResponse()                                                                                                                       │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ response.append_chunk(                                                                                                                          │
│     ToolChunk(                                                                                                                                  │
│         content=[                                                                                                                               │
│             DataBlock(                                                                                                                          │
│                 id="image",                                                                                                                     │
│                 source=Base64Source(                                                                                                            │
│                     data=base64.b64encode(b"hello").decode("ascii"),                                                                            │
│                     media_type="image/png",                                                                                                     │
│                 ),                                                                                                                              │
│             ),                                                                                                                                  │
│         ],                                                                                                                                      │
│     ),                                                                                                                                          │
│ )                                                                                                                                               │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ response.append_chunk(                                                                                                                          │
│     ToolChunk(                                                                                                                                  │
│         content=[                                                                                                                               │
│             DataBlock(                                                                                                                          │
│                 id="image",                                                                                                                     │
│                 source=Base64Source(                                                                                                            │
│                     data=base64.b64encode(b"world").decode("ascii"),                                                                            │
│                     media_type="image/png",                                                                                                     │
│                 ),                                                                                                                              │
│             ),                                                                                                                                  │
│         ],                                                                                                                                      │
│     ),                                                                                                                                          │
│ )                                                                                                                                               │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ merged = response.content[0].source.data                                                                                                        │
│ print(merged)                                                                                                                                   │
│ print(base64.b64decode(merged))                                                                                                                 │
│ ```                                                                                                                                             │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ 2. Observe that the merged base64 string is produced by direct string concatenation.                                                            │
│ 3. The decoded payload is incomplete and does not contain both chunks.                                                                          │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ ### Environment                                                                                                                                 │
│                                                                                                                                                 │
│ - AgentScope Version: 2.0.3 / current main branch                                                                                               │
│ - Python Version: 3.13.3                                                                                                                        │
│ - OS: macOS                                                                                                                                     │
